# ALLOWLIST build context (positive-list basis).
#
# The `*` rule below excludes EVERYTHING from the build context. Anything the
# image build genuinely needs must be re-included with an explicit `!pattern`
# line in the ALLOWLIST section — one deliberate, reviewable line per item.
# Never weaken the `*` itself.
#
# The allowlist is currently EMPTY by design: the Containerfile has no
# COPY/ADD (app code is volume-mounted at runtime), and the Containerfile
# itself is always sent to the builder regardless of these rules. This
# guarantees runtime secrets and PII (.env, personalinfo.md, .chrome-profile,
# .claude) can never enter the context tarball or a published image — and any
# future COPY fails loudly at build time until its source is allowlisted here.
#
# Read by docker directly and by podman (which falls back to .dockerignore
# when no .containerignore exists).

# Deny everything…
*

# ── ALLOWLIST — re-include build inputs below, one `!` line each ──────────
# (empty — no COPY directives in the Containerfile)
# Example:  !entrypoint.sh
